AtomEngine Demo @PROJECT_VERSION@
=====================================

A first-person walk through a foggy rural Japanese street in the spirit
of 2000s horror and, a night bus ride away, one street of a neon city -
2000s-inspired art direction on a modern renderer.

Start: double-click Demo.exe. Nothing to install.
Needs: Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit) and a Direct3D 12 GPU.

Controls
--------
  WASD / Shift / Mouse   move / jog / look
  E                      interact; in dialogue: continue / confirm
  W S or 1-4             choose a dialogue option
  F                      flashlight (once found)
  Esc                    release the mouse (again: quit)
  F2 - F8                render scale, baked light, MSAA, fog, shadows,
                         post look, particles
  M                      mute

At the pachinko machine: hold Space to launch, Up / Down (or the mouse
wheel) for strength, B or Enter to buy balls, Q or Backspace to stand up.

Settings and logs
-----------------
Settings (chosen with the options below) and the log of each run are
kept per user, not in this folder:

  %APPDATA%\AtomEngine\Demo\settings.json
  %APPDATA%\AtomEngine\Demo\logs\Demo.log      (this run)
  %APPDATA%\AtomEngine\Demo\logs\Demo.previous.log

If it doesn't start
-------------------
A message names the reason and the log. Useful to try, from a terminal
in this folder:

  Demo.exe --gpu low-power        the integrated GPU (laptops)
  Demo.exe --quality low          lighter rendering
  Demo.exe --reset-settings       back to the defaults
  Demo.exe --diagnostics report.txt
                                  writes what the game found (GPU,
                                  display, settings) and quits

When reporting a problem, send Demo.log and that report.

